      "problem": "Given that $\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  =x$ and $\\dfrac {2a} {14b^2}=y,$ then what is $x \\div y?$",
      "worked_solution": "To compute\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  &\\div  \\dfrac {2a} {14b^2},\n\t}\n$$\n\nwe just need to multiply by the reciprocal of the divisor:\n\n$$\n\\require{cancel}\n\t\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  \\div  \\dfrac {2a} {14b^2}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a^3 - 10a} {7b}  \\cdot \\dfrac {14b^2} {2a}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {2a(a^2 - 5)} {7b}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {2b \\cdot 7b} {2a}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {\\cancel{2a}(a^2 - 5)} {\\cancel{7b}}  \\cdot  \\dfrac {2b \\cdot \\cancel{7b}} {\\cancel{2a}}&=\\\n\t\t\\dfrac {2b(a^2 - 5)} 1 &=\\\n\t\t2a^2b - 10b &\n\t}\n$$",
